The schema is published as an open specification and resolves at its own $id,
https://freshcontext.dev/freshcontext.schema.json, so that other people's
validators can fetch it. It is a mirror of the canonical copy in
freshcontext-mcp, which is MIT throughout. The two must agree, and CI checks
that they do.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. Everything else in this repository — all rights reserved

Copyright (c) 2026 Immanuel Gabriel. All rights reserved.

The page copy, layout, stylesheets, imagery and brand assets are not open
source and are not licensed for reuse. Being able to read them in a public
repository is not permission to republish them. See TRADEMARKS.md in
freshcontext-mcp for the position on the FreshContext name and marks.

This split is deliberate. The specification is meant to be adopted; the site
that describes it is not meant to be cloned.
